WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.630
Writing is a way of contributing
to the political climate

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:06.600
and saying something meaningful,
because not all of us

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.893
are going to run for office.

00:00:07.893 --> 00:00:09.310
I'm never going
to run for office.

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:10.500
My past is filthy.

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:14.800
Writing is such a great
career, but you definitely

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.870
don't need to be a writer
to enjoy this class.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.280
For one, I'm
incredibly charming.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:23.290
Writing has always
influenced public opinion.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.450
It's one of the
most effective means

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.730
of reaching a great
number of people

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.820
and to get other people on
board with progressive ideas

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.880
like women are people
and Black Lives Matter,

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.100
and everyone should
have health care.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.960
I know that these are
very radical ideas,

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:39.880
but writing for social
change is really

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.160
just writing to make a
difference in this world.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.680
In this MasterClass,
you're going

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.000
to learn how to write better,
think deeper, and contribute

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.370
your voice to the
world in valuable ways;

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:56.950
and we're going to talk about
the business of publishing

00:00:56.950 --> 00:01:00.335
and how to really get a start.

00:01:00.335 --> 00:01:01.960
One of the things
that we should always

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.180
try to do as writers
is to figure out

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:07.805
what can you bring to this
discussion that no one else

00:01:07.805 --> 00:01:08.305
can.

00:01:08.305 --> 00:01:10.210
 I mean, that feels
more fun to me.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:11.050
 Isn't it more fun?

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:13.024
 Yeah.

00:01:13.024 --> 00:01:15.310
 Perfection is not the
goal when you're writing,

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.090
excellence is.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:20.360
"Hunger" is a memoir that
I wrote about my body,

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:22.730
and it starts with a sexual
assault I experienced when

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:26.180
I was 12, and I turned to
food as a source of comfort

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.250
and as a source of
protection, thinking

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:31.250
that if I made myself
bigger, I would become safer.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:32.930
"My body is a cage.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:35.120
My body is a cage
of my own making.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:37.340
I'm still trying to
figure my way out of it.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.140
I have been trying
to figure my way out

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:42.120
of it for more than 20 years."

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.712
It was a very difficult book
to write because I was afraid.

00:01:44.712 --> 00:01:46.670
You don't need to be
brave when you're writing.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:49.010
You need to acknowledge
that you're terrified,

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:50.545
and do it anyway.

00:01:50.545 --> 00:01:52.420
But don't think that
trauma is the only thing

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.510
you have to offer.

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.330
You can write about anything.

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:58.480
Writing, for a lot of people,
ends up being salvation,

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.260
and when writing finds you,
when writing saves you,

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:04.990
it opens up a whole new
world of possibility,

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:09.380
and I hope that certainly
is the case for you.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:14.350
I'm Roxane Gay, and
this is my MasterClass.

